# data-models-relationships

## Core Data Models

### Treatment Facility Model
Importance Score: 95
- Multi-tiered classification system:
  - Population served (coed, gender-specific, families)
  - Treatment levels (detox, residential, outpatient)
  - Insurance acceptance (Medi-Cal, Medicare, private)
- County-specific jurisdictional relationships
- Verification status workflow tracking

### Legal Case Model 
Importance Score: 90
- Case type taxonomy:
  - Custody reunification 
  - Record expungement
  - Benefits appeals
- Milestone tracking with type-specific templates
- Document requirements by case stage
- Relationship mapping to appointments/deadlines

### Resource Location Model
Importance Score: 85
- Hierarchical categorization:
  - Safe zones
  - Resource centers
  - Basic needs (food/water)
  - Emergency services
- Community verification status tracking
- Real-time availability updates
- Geographic relationship mapping

### Medical Provider Model
Importance Score: 80
- Specialty taxonomy mapping
- Network affiliation tracking
- Language service relationships
- Insurance acceptance verification
- Geographic service area definitions

## Key Relationships

### Verification Workflows
- Three-tier verification system:
  1. Community submission
  2. Peer verification
  3. Official validation
- Status tracking across all resource types
- Change history maintenance
- Update authority levels

### Service Area Mappings
- County-level jurisdiction tracking
- Resource coverage analysis
- Service overlap detection
- Accessibility relationship scoring

### Crisis Response Integration
- Emergency resource availability links
- Service provider on-call status
- Response team jurisdiction mapping
- Resource allocation relationships

